{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal: distinguish the edge, of the four candidates the request names.\n\nOnly a describes relation propagates world-staleness. A general rests_on records what an act was reasoned from and what occasioned it, and a death upstream of that means only that the reasoning happened at an earlier state. Multi-hop reach is kept for describes edges, because it catches the real drift the convention was ratified for: a page describing behaviour must still flare when that behaviour changes, however many hops away the change lands.\n\nEvidence from 2026-08-09, offered because the request asks for both directions demonstrated on the real log rather than on fixtures. Four independent pieces of work were blocked in one morning by staleness that carried no information: a UI request resting on the merge artifact for main at 2757411d, and its promise, artifact, report and review request, all flared when a later merge superseded that artifact, and gs review then refused the artifact outright so the work could not be reviewed until it was re-anchored. The same pattern cost a full reintegration on the kernel rotation line and a re-issue on two others. In none of the four had any described behaviour changed. Against that, the flare that must be kept: a document describing behaviour whose implementation artifact is superseded at merge, which is the case the ratified convention exists to catch.\n\nWhat existing history means under the new reading, which the request requires be said plainly: every act already written used the single edge, so every existing rests_on is read as the general relation and propagates nothing. Describes edges exist only from adoption forward. That is the conservative reading — it under-flares old acts rather than inventing describes relations nobody declared — and it means the convention's guarantee holds for documents written after adoption, not retroactively. An author who wants an existing page covered restates its artifact with an explicit describes edge.\n\nI have separately filed two child requests for the parts that do not depend on this ratification: the review gate conflating retired with stale, and merge artifacts claiming path dot. Neither changes the schema and both can land first."}